.TH GEO-DOWNLOAD 1 "2026-10-28" "geo-download 1.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
geo-download \- download a country's IP blocks as aggregated CIDR subnets
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B geo-download
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOUNTRY\fR...
.br
.B geo-download
\fB\-\-check\fR \fIPATH\fR
.br
.B geo-download
\fB\-\-completion\fR {\fBbash\fR|\fBzsh\fR}
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B geo-download
fetches the IP address blocks registered to one or more countries, merges
overlapping and adjacent ranges into the smallest possible set of CIDR
subnets and writes the result to a text file with one subnet per line.
.PP
Two public data sources are used: \fIipverse/rir-ip\fR (derived from RIR
delegation files) by default, with \fIipdeny.com\fR as a fallback.
.PP
Human-readable messages, warnings and the progress bar are written to
standard error. Standard output carries only the generated list, and only
when \fB\-\-stdout\fR is given.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fIPATH\fR
Write the list to \fIPATH\fR instead of \fI<country>.txt\fR. Valid for a single
country only.
.TP
\fB\-\-stdout\fR
Write the rendered list to standard output instead of a file. Valid for a
single country only.
.TP
\fB\-\-family\fR {\fB4\fR|\fB6\fR|\fBboth\fR}
Address family to download. Default: \fB4\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv6\fR
Alias for \fB\-\-family both\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-source\fR {\fBauto\fR|\fBipverse\fR|\fBipdeny\fR}
Data source. Default: \fBauto\fR, which tries \fBipverse\fR first.
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fISECONDS\fR
Socket timeout per request. Default: 30.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR {\fBplain\fR|\fBipset\fR|\fBnft\fR|\fBnginx\fR|\fBjson\fR}
Output format. Default: \fBplain\fR.
.RS
.TP
\fBplain\fR
One CIDR subnet per line.
.TP
\fBipset\fR
\fBadd \fISET\fR \fISUBNET\fR\fR lines, suitable for \fBipset restore\fR.
.TP
\fBnft\fR
A brace-delimited nftables element list.
.TP
\fBnginx\fR
\fBallow \fISUBNET\fR;\fR lines.
.TP
\fBjson\fR
A JSON object with \fBipv4\fR, \fBipv6\fR, counters and the total address
count.
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-set\-name\fR \fINAME\fR
Set name used by \fB\-\-format ipset\fR. Default: the lowercase country code.
.TP
\fB\-\-with\-header\fR
Prepend comment lines describing the generator version, country, source and
generation time. Not supported by \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-exclude\fR \fICIDR\fR
Remove a network from the result. May be repeated.
.TP
\fB\-\-exclude\-file\fR \fIPATH\fR
Read networks to remove from \fIPATH\fR, one per line. Blank lines and
\fB#\fR comments are ignored.
.TP
\fB\-\-min\-prefix\fR \fIN\fR
Drop networks broader than \fI/N\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-prefix\fR \fIN\fR
Drop networks smaller than \fI/N\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-if\-changed\fR
Leave the output file untouched when its content is already identical.
.TP
\fB\-\-exit\-code\-changed\fR
With \fB\-\-if\-changed\fR, exit with status 3 when nothing was written.
.TP
\fB\-\-diff\fR \fIPATH\fR
Print the networks added or removed compared to \fIPATH\fR before writing.
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fR \fIPATH\fR
Validate an existing block list without accessing the network. Reports
unparsable lines, duplicates and overlapping networks; exits non-zero when
problems are found.
.TP
\fB\-\-cache\-dir\fR \fIPATH\fR
Enable an HTTP cache in \fIPATH\fR. Requests are revalidated with
\fBETag\fR/\fBLast\-Modified\fR headers, so unchanged upstream files are not
transferred again.
.TP
\fB\-\-completion\fR {\fBbash\fR|\fBzsh\fR}
Print a shell completion script to standard output and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-progress\fR
Disable the progress bar. It is disabled automatically when standard error is
not a terminal.
.TP
\fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress informational output. Errors are still reported.
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Print the version and exit.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print usage information and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Download, filtering or write failure, or \fB\-\-check\fR found problems.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command line arguments.
.TP
.B 3
\fB\-\-if\-changed\fR was used with \fB\-\-exit\-code\-changed\fR and the file was
already up to date.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted by SIGINT.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Any non-empty value disables ANSI colors.
.TP
.B TERM
\fBTERM=dumb\fR disables ANSI colors.
.TP
.B HTTPS_PROXY\fR, \fBHTTP_PROXY\fR, \fBNO_PROXY
Honored by the underlying \fBurllib\fR implementation.
.SH EXAMPLES
Write the Turkish IPv4 blocks to \fItr.txt\fR:
.PP
.RS
geo-download tr
.RE
.PP
Refresh daily from cron and only reload the firewall when the list changed:
.PP
.RS
17 4 * * * cd /srv/geoip && geo-download tr --quiet --if-changed --exit-code-changed || nft \-f apply.nft
.RE
.PP
Feed the Turkish blocks directly into an ipset:
.PP
.RS
geo-download tr --format ipset --set\-name tr4 --stdout | ipset restore \-exist
.RE
.SH LIMITATIONS
The generated list reflects registry delegations, not physical location.
Anycast, VPN, satellite and mobile roaming traffic will not match
expectations, and delegation data lags real-world reassignment.
.PP
Set-oriented formats (\fBipset\fR, \fBnft\fR) are single-family in practice;
run them once per address family when both families are needed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ipset (8),
.BR nft (8),
.BR iptables (8)
